# Roundup's classhelper popups render the `property` and `form` query
# parameters into a `<script>` element through a ZPT `tal:content` whose
# expression carries the `structure` modifier, so the interpolated values
# reach the page unescaped and a crafted `?@template=help&property=</
# script><script>...` URL executes in the popup. `structure` is ZPT's
# documented "emit the result without HTML quoting" switch; the fixing commit
# drops it from twenty-four attribute values across the five shipped tracker
# templates plus the website issue tracker and leaves the interpolations
# themselves untouched, so the discriminating fact is the modifier, not any
# value. The same commit's roundup/cgi/client.py hunks belong to two other
# advisories in the same release (a Referer reflected through an unescaped
# error message, and a Content-Security-Policy on downloads), so the pool
# row's `python` language field names the repository rather than the file the
# fixed revision lands in.
#
# ZPT writes this weakness as an attribute value that spans lines: the
# `structure string:` opener sits on the element's start-tag line and the
# `${request/form/...}` interpolation two or three lines below, so a rule
# evaluated against one physical line can never see both halves. The text
# template scopes now also match rules against the attribute value as a
# unit, which is what makes the pair expressible: a `tal:content` value that
# carries the `structure` modifier on a `string:` expression and interpolates
# something is a stored HTML write, and the ordinary widget form
# `structure context/username/field` -- the same modifier on a traversal
# expression that the templating engine renders as a built field widget --
# carries no interpolation and does not match.
#
# Measured on the real checkout at the fixing commit's parent and at the fix:
# the tracker templates report 45 VYQL-INJ-028 before and 27 after, three
# runs each and identical every time, against a baseline of 25 on both sides
# from the jinja2 family's `|safe` filters. The twenty added rows are exactly
# the twenty classhelper attributes the fix edits; the two that survive the
# fix are milestone.item.html's `structure string:Created on
# <b>${context/creation}</b>...` renders, which the fix does not touch and
# which interpolate traversal expressions rather than request paths. No other
# rule's count moves. The needle fires on no file of either benchmark corpus
# and on none of the other ZPT trees in the corpus (Zope's own PageTemplates
# and CMFPlone), because those carry no `structure string:` interpolation.

test "rank1686: a classhelper popup renders request parameters into a script element with the structure modifier"
  lang config
  file _generic.help.html
  expect VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <html tal:define="property request/form/property/value | nothing">
    <head>
      <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="@@file/style.css" />
      <tal:block tal:condition="python:'property' in request.form">
      <title><tal:x tal:content="property | default" i18n:translate="" /> help</title>
      <script language="Javascript" type="text/javascript"
          tal:content="structure string:
          // this is the name of the field in the original form that we're working on
          form  = window.opener.document.${request/form/form/value};
          field  = '${request/form/property/value}';">
      </script>
      </tal:block>
    </head>
   <body class="body" onload="resetList();">
   <form name="frm_help" tal:attributes="action request/base"
         tal:define="props python:request.form['properties'].value.split(',')">
     <input type="text" name="text_preview" size="24" class="preview"
            onchange="reviseList(this.value);"/>
   </form>
   </body>
  </html>
  ```

test "rank1686: the classhelper popup escapes the interpolated script block"
  lang config
  file _generic.help.html
  reject VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <html tal:define="property request/form/property/value | nothing">
    <head>
      <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="@@file/style.css" />
      <tal:block tal:condition="python:'property' in request.form">
      <title><tal:x tal:content="property | default" i18n:translate="" /> help</title>
      <script language="Javascript" type="text/javascript"
          tal:content="string:
          // this is the name of the field in the original form that we're working on
          form  = window.opener.document.${request/form/form/value};
          field  = '${request/form/property/value}';">
      </script>
      </tal:block>
    </head>
   <body class="body" onload="resetList();">
   <form name="frm_help" tal:attributes="action request/base"
         tal:define="props python:request.form['properties'].value.split(',')">
     <input type="text" name="text_preview" size="24" class="preview"
            onchange="reviseList(this.value);"/>
   </form>
   </body>
  </html>
  ```

test "rank1686: a helper that hands a built field widget through keeps the structure modifier"
  lang config
  file user.register.html
  reject VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <html tal:define="property request/form/property/value | nothing">
    <head>
      <title>Register</title>
    </head>
   <body class="body">
   <form method="POST" name="itemSynopsis"
         tal:attributes="action context/designator">
   <table class="form">
    <tr>
     <th i18n:translate="">Username</th>
     <td tal:content="structure context/username/field">username</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
     <th i18n:translate="">Password</th>
     <td tal:content="structure context/password/field">password</td>
    </tr>
   </table>
   </form>
   </body>
  </html>
  ```
